{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502522-aggravated-damage-and-scarring","id":1502522,"title":"Aggravated damage and scarring","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-08T11:25:20-08:00","id":1502522,"title":"Aggravated damage and scarring","content":"I recall reading that aggravated damage could leave scars and was wondering if I was hallucinating and what others thought of the concept. (It was the Storyteller's Handbook, I think.) <br /> Pretty sure that was one of those things that was briefly thought up once and then forgotten by everyone as the setting moved on, but it stuck with me.<br /> If that's the case then fire, sunlight, fangs and claws are no longer simply a bitch to heal, they never truly do, a mark on your otherwise static form and a reminder that you absolutely can still suffer permanent consequences (like death).<br /> <br /> On the one hand, one might feel it detracts from the curse. The inescapable stasis that cuts vampires off from the world.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I enjoy the threat of permanency and feel like it also has interesting applications. It'd be interesting to incorporate into punishments or ritae, for example.<br /> You could be marked with proof of a crime/disgrace so that everyone knows your shame for eternity. Branded by your sire as property.<br /> Your sire got bored of you and left you for his new childe? Burn her pretty face off. <br /> Packmates could share ritual scarifications or a sigil of unity branded into their flesh for all eternity. <br /> If a gangrel hacks their hair off with feral claws, does it grow back? What if your hair catches fire?<br /> If you find a way to make needles inflict aggravated, can you do tattoos and piercings? I mean, the Tremere have adapted a branding ritual for body art, so it's not that big of a stretch.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T13:43:23-08:00","id":1502536,"title":"","content":"I ignore this, because if it's so, then every vampire over a couple hundred years old should be as ugly as a Nosferatu. No way do you go more than a couple hundred years without taking even one close-call blast of sunlight to the face, get one splash of burning oil to the face, get in one fight where another vampire ripped a chunk out of your face with its teeth, have one priest with true faith shove a cross in your face or splash you with holy water, have one Gangrel or werewolf claw you, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> A really political character might go fifty, even a hundred years without any of those things happening if he's super-political and really lucky, but he aint going multiple centuries, I don't buy it. Vampires are predators with very dangerous prey, with vampiric rivals who want them assassinated, can take burn damage every single day simply by losing track of the time, and live in houses that are just as flammable as anyone else's house.<br /> <br /> Agg damage is a fact of life for these predators, and if it never healed, then all elders should be as ugly as the Nos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T17:16:38-08:00","id":1502550,"title":"","content":"In the Revised Edition <b>Storyteller's Handbook</b>, on page 20, the question was asked, <b>To what extent does a vampire's body revert to its original form each day while he sleeps?</b><br /> <br /> The answer goes on to explain that changes which do not cause damage enough to be marked as heath levels on your character sheet are healed automatically during the day while they sleep. If the change is significant and can be marked as health levels on your character sheet, then the changes will revert upon the healing of those health levels.<br /> <br /> Finally, in a stand-alone statement, and no where else in the material - during that time or since - it says, A<i>ggravated damage, even when healed, almost always leaves a telling scar.</i><br /> <br /> Because it is never mentioned in the system, many are either unaware or have decided to ignore it. Personally, I have always enjoyed using it for many of the reasons you already listed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27764,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27764-hasnamuss","user":"Hasnamuss","date":". 02-08-2023, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27764-hasnamuss","name":"Hasnamuss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27764_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T17:57:31-08:00","id":1502559,"title":"","content":"Anything that can permanently damage an immortal and is at all routinely encountered creates the problem that eventually all immortals will be massively permanently damaged.<br /> <br /> I mean, are we seriously supposed to accept that not once in her 800 years as a warrior, has Lucita ever eaten aggs to the face?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 02-08-2023, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T18:16:28-08:00","id":1502561,"title":"","content":"Personally, I give the player the choice of whether it leaves a scar. You might make the player roll Stamina against an arbitrary difficulty to see if it leaves a scar too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T21:52:54-08:00","id":1502587,"title":"","content":"I would have no problem with aggravated damage leaving permanent scars for mortals or Garou, but I think vampires should always heal back to their original embraced form. I am heavily in agreement with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3598_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3598\" data-vbnamecard=\"3598\">CajunKhan</a>. At the same time, if for some reason the the cause of the aggravated wounds is exceptional and per <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27252\" data-vbnamecard=\"27252\">Hades</a> the character wanted a scar as a reminder for some reason, I would not be against it. I would not have it be the normal result. It's just flavor text when warranted.<br /> <br /> Aggravated damage is just too common for it to leave permanent reminders on vampires. It just goes against most genre conventions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T22:41:01-08:00","id":1502589,"title":"","content":"From time to time, you can see the inspirations of the original game float to the surface. The aggravated damage leaving an identifying scar is most likely a holdover from the first Highlander movie when the Kurgan gets his iconic throat scar which never goes away despite immortals always healing perfectly.<br /> <br /> I don't enforce the rule, unless the Player wants to use it as a story point for their character or I want an NPC to really hold a grudge. I will say that by keeping this concept around, it can cause players to consider head on confrontations a bit more rather than recklessly running in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T23:17:10-08:00","id":1502591,"title":"","content":"I wasn't aware there was such a rule, and now that I am, I will safely ignore it. Imagine sunlight did this: Your five-appearance face suffers horrible scaring (including your eyes) because that one time someone opened the curtains. Just doesn't sound reasonable to me. <br /> <br /> Brand exists as a ritual<br /> Flesh of the corpse exists as a flaw. <br /> <br /> There's no need for it. Maybe as something like &quot;in healing an agg wound you used 4 blood rather than 5 and lose the mechanical damage but keep a scar till you finish healing...&quot; but as a general consequence of normal agg? No. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-10T11:15:40-08:00","id":1502700,"title":"","content":"I'd just go with the VTR first edition rules where the vampire gives up a willpower dot to keep a scar as a reminder of a failure. Otherwise they just revert back to there default form each night when they wake up from there day sleep and such.<br /> <br /> I.E. my Malkavian scholar might keep a scar as a reminder not to get tunnel vision and put himself in a situation that he can't get out of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 02-10-2023, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T18:02:46-08:00","id":1502798,"title":"","content":"I tend to treat it like the effects of the initial embrace on wounds and imperfections. Sometimes everything heals up fine, sometimes it leaves a mark\u2014whatever's dramatically interesting. No one knows for sure why it happens that way.<br /> <br /> I'm not necessarily opposed to the idea of really old vampires taking on disturbing appearances as they grow centuries old and further away from humanity. Something happened to Ur-Shulgi, for example, and most methuselahs are so far removed from humanity that I don't think it would hamper them too much to reflect it in their appearance. Hey, it worked on <i>Buffy</i>!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T02:45:50-08:00","id":1502819,"title":"","content":"I'd go with &quot;If you were ever incapacitated by Aggravated&quot; it will leave a mark. Not necessarily to the extent it would on a human, but there would be some kind of tally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T07:39:53-08:00","id":1502837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502522-aggravated-damage-and-scarring?p=1502591#post1502591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brand exists as a ritual<br /> Flesh of the corpse exists as a flaw.</div> </div> </div> </div>^This. I generally think if it would invalidate another aspect of the game design, it's probably not intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T10:58:08-08:00","id":1503389,"title":"","content":"I think Urgi Shurgi was disfigured before he was embraced by Haqim if I recall the revised Assamite clanbook correctly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}